    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to bolster our 5x5 standing. Our strongest play is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who sits at the top of the board due to a prime leadoff spot and a high-leverage matchup against Ober. The combination of Ober\u2019s susceptibility to stolen bases\u2014highlighted by a slow delivery\u2014and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s elite speed makes him an essential anchor for our SB category today. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (72.74) is a must-start, benefiting from a dynamic platoon advantage against Alcantara, while **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) earns a high projection by leveraging a significant platoon edge and a favorable #3 slot against Kay.\n\nWe are playing the matchups aggressively, particularly with **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Junior Caminero** (65.86), both of whom see their floor raised by favorable park factors and high-leverage order placement. While **Yordan Alvarez** (59.18) carries a lower score than usual due to a difficult matchup against the pitcher, his elite xwOBA remains a stabilizing force for our offensive output. The most difficult decision at the margins involved **Colt Keith** (44.29); he was the final cut from our starting nine, ultimately benched because of a restrictive platoon disadvantage against a left-handed arm in Detmers. While his base projection was solid, the optimizer prioritized the higher efficiency scores of our other starters to maintain our category ceilings.\n\nManagers should remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several of our key assets, including **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Luke Raley**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Lars Nootbaar**. These projected positions are based on historical trends, and any late-breaking lineup shifts could necessitate a recalibration of our efficiency targets. We are currently sitting above the Zebras' 40-point floor for all starters, ensuring that we maximize our game-day utility without wasting precious caps on marginal bench options like **Chase Meidroth** or **Jacob Gonzalez**, who remain sidelined as they failed to meet our aggressive efficiency threshold.",
